Content follows common Vaishnava observance: Devshayani (Ashadhi) Ekadashi begins Chaturmas, the four monsoon months of
Vishnu's sleep; Prabodhini (Kartiki) Ekadashi marks his waking; Tulsi Vivah is celebrated around that day (customs vary by region),
and the wedding season follows. Months are given as their usual Gregorian ranges; exact dates follow the lunar calendar each year.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
